; BrailleMonitor.inix -- how this database opens, and how its tables are heard.
;
; THE BRAILLE MONITOR, SEARCHABLE. Every issue of the National Federation of the Blind's magazine that nfb.org offers,
; from 1957 on: one row an issue in issues, one row an article in articles. Every Monitor article is its own web page
; at nfb.org, so its words are in body as Markdown, with the NFB's own headings, lists and links. search_text holds
; the same words with no markup and no link addresses: the full-text index reads it, not body, so a search and the
; passage it reads aloud carry no Markdown. The database is made the same way as BrailleForum, by the same code.
;
; FIND ONE. The row speaks title, writer and published (the year and month). Keywords (Control+K) and Filter Records
; work as on any table; Full-text match in Filter Records uses the index. The saved searches here rank their matches
; and read the passage that matched; the BrailleMonitor part of DbDo's guide shows the forms a search takes.
;
; READ ONE. Alt+Right on an issue goes to its articles, in the issue's order (position). Control+Shift+H, Preview Markdown in Web
; Browser, shows the article as a web page; Control+Shift+U opens it at nfb.org. The reading_list report writes up marked articles.
;
; WRITERS. One row a person, from every byline; each article is mapped to each of its writers (maps, written_by),
; so Alt+Right goes from a writer to their articles and from an article to its writers.
;
; scripts\makeBrailleMonitor in DbDo's development folder builds this file from nfb.org; the build runs it when the
; database is missing. The database stays on that computer: it is not on GitHub and not in the installer.

[Database]
; A REFERENCE DATABASE (26 November 2026): rebuilt from the magazine, so the copy DbDo opens follows each newer
; build, replaced whenever this template is newer. Notes, tags or marks made in the copy go with it.
FollowTemplate = yes

InitialTable = articles

[Table:articles]

SelectFields = title, writer, published

[Table:writers]

SelectFields = name, articles, last_published

[Table:issues]

SelectFields = title, articles, words

[Table:defs]


[Table:maps]
